// REJECTS: Unexpected token ''localhost:27017''
//
// `serverURLs: ['localhost:27017'];` with the entries QUOTED. The rule is
//     serverURL : HOST_STRING COLON INTEGER
// -- a bare host token and a bare integer, no string literal anywhere -- so the quoted form
// that every other list of endpoints in this corpus uses is refused here.
//
// The value of the fixture is the collision with its own section. MongoDBSchemaLexerGrammar
// makes double quotes the string form and single quotes invalid
// (./neg-mongodb-single-quoted-jsonschema.pure); MongoDBConnectionLexerGrammar makes the host
// list take NO quotes of either kind. Three quoting conventions inside one vendor, chosen per
// grammar file, and a rewrite that unifies them is more permissive in every direction at once.
//
// The port is part of the grammar rather than a separate field, so `serverURLs: [localhost];`
// does not parse either -- the COLON INTEGER is mandatory.
###Connection
MongoDBConnection fixture::neg::QuotedServerUrls
{
  database: legend_db;
  store: fixture::neg::Db;
  serverURLs: ['localhost:27017'];
  authentication: # Kerberos { }#;
}
